WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.843
Unit twenty-two. Incident Response!

2
00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:09.242
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:12.898
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:16.816
Today we learn about Incident Response. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:21.830
Incident. Say it with me. Incident!

6
00:00:25.346 --> 00:00:28.879
Detect. Say it with me. Detect!

7
00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.128
Contain. Say it with me. Contain!

8
00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:43.632
Investigate. Say it with me. Investigate!

9
00:00:47.141 --> 00:00:51.006
Recover. Say it with me. Recover!

10
00:00:54.465 --> 00:00:58.098
Report. Say it with me. Report!

11
00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:04.993
Plan. Say it with me. Plan!

12
00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:12.955
Lessons learned. Say it with me. Lessons learned!

13
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:27.847
When a security incident happens, teams detect it, contain the damage, investigate, and recover. They report to the right people and follow a plan, then record lessons learned.

14
00:01:27.897 --> 00:01:31.402
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:37.424
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:37.474 --> 00:01:38.624
Contain!

17
00:01:39.591 --> 00:01:44.770
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.970
Plan!

19
00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:53.324
Did you know? Practising incident response with drills helps teams react faster in real attacks!

20
00:01:53.374 --> 00:01:55.693
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:05.571
Think and answer. Why is having a plan important before an incident?

22
00:02:05.621 --> 00:02:06.771
Great answer!

23
00:02:08.034 --> 00:02:13.156
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:16.279
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

